From 4505fd2a580ad3a6b07fd6c02c999e43668708b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duy Khanh Tran <kanetran29@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:20:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] angular: scope attribution for shared components and the app
 shell

Adds an opt-in attribution pass (--attribution). Components are linked by
element selector (import-narrowed when ambiguous); route components render
on their subtree; the unrouted outlet holder is the shell (scope top).
Edges whose screen set is top or a whole subtree are stored once at a
'scope' node and expanded on query (core: edgesFrom, expandAnchoredEdges).
Indirect shells (no visible mounting route) are capped at may.

Also: merged witnesses for constructs that produce an existing edge, and
inline-template witnesses now point at the construct's own line. With the
option off, the graph is identical to the baseline on all six corpus apps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01V7vUBgQMTagyrjSYx1vQVk
